    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0349" n="253" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg253"/>

                <head>No. 205.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Francis to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 3, 1872</date>.
                        (Received August 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 69.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    translation of a communication <pb facs="0350" n="254" xml:id="pg254"/> this day
                    received from Mr. Bulgaris, minister of foreign affairs, expressing the cordial
                    thanks of the Greek government for the reduction of the duty on Corinth grapes
                    (dried currants) by the Congress of the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c., &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN M. FRANCIS.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d205-a1.xml" xpointer="d205-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
